// core-lib-03: CachedArgs re-runs eval on every stale update while its last
// result is bottom (update_inner's last arm), so a standing div0 logs once per
// cycle its statement updates, against design/dense_delivery.md "Builtin seams"
// (retag STALE without eval on a stale join) and ruled delta 6 (standing
// bottoms never log).
// command: RUST_LOG=error graphix --no-cache --no-fusion --log-dir DIR core-lib-03.gx 2>&1 | grep -c divide
// expected: 1 (divide's args fire only at init; `10 / b` in its place logs once)
// observed: 22 (init + one per ep cycle; 7 with `n < 5`), same with fusion on
let b = 0;
let ep = 0;
ep <- select ep { n if n < 20 => n + 1, _ => never() };
let t = (ep, divide(10, b));
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:200.ms, 0));
ep
